  "raw_text": "Step 1: Calculate the amount Kathy will withdraw in British pounds.\nStep 2: Calculate the amount Kathy will withdraw in euros.\nStep 3: Convert the amount withdrawn in British pounds to USD.\nStep 4: Convert the amount withdrawn in euros to USD.\nStep 5: Find the difference between the amounts in euros and pounds in USD.\nStep 6: Round the difference to the nearest whole number.\n\nStep 1: The amount Kathy will withdraw in British pounds is half of 300 USD, which is \\(300 / 2 = 150\\) USD.\n\nStep 2: The amount Kathy will withdraw in euros is also half of 300 USD, which is \\(300 / 2 = 150\\) USD.\n\nStep 3: To convert the amount withdrawn in British pounds to USD, we use the conversion rate 1 pound = 1.64 USD. So, \\(150\\) pounds is equivalent to \\(150 / 1.64 \\approx 91.41\\) USD.\n\nStep 4: To convert the amount withdrawn in euros to USD, we use the conversion rate 1 euro = 1.32 USD. So, \\(150\\) euros is equivalent to \\(150 / 1.32 \\approx 113.64\\) USD.\n\nStep 5: The difference between the amounts in euros and pounds in USD is \\(113.64 - 91.41 = 22.23\\) USD.\n\nStep 6: Rounding 22.23 to the nearest whole number gives us 22.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{22}<|im_end|>",
  "reforward_peak_bytes": 15464599552,
